---
title: Spanakopita
source: https://www.theguardian.com/food/2018/aug/22/how-to-cook-the-perfect-spanakopita-greek-spinach-feta-pie
servings: 6
course: Starter
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
---

If fresh @spinach{1%kg}(or frozen spinach, defrosted) is being used: Trim the spinach and wash well, then roughly chop. Put in a colander with a good sprinkle of @salt, and massage until it wilts.

Gently fry the @leek or red onion{1}(finely chopped) in the @olive oil{2%tbsp} until softened, then take off the heat and stir in the @spring onions{4}(chopped). Tip into a very large bowl with the @feta{300%g}(crumbled), herbs (@dill{25%g}(chopped), @mint{20%g}(leaves removed and chopped), and @oregano{3%sprigs}(chopped)), and (if using) @?bulgur wheat{50%g}.

Wring the spinach in handfuls until no more liquid comes out, and then stir into the cheese mix. Add the @eggs{2}(beaten), @lemon{1}(zest only), a glug of oil, and a good grating of @nutmeg. Mix again (hands are the best tool for this). Season lightly, remembering that feta is quite salty.

Heat the oven to 200°C. Brush a #30 cm x 25 cm baking tin{} with @olive oil{}. Line the tin with half the @filo pastry{250%g}, brushing each sheet with oil, and taking care not to press them down in the process. Leave any excess overhanging the sides.

Spoon in the filling and level the top. Repeat the layering process with the remaining pastry. Fold the overhang inwards, to make an edible rim, and drizzle with more oil. Cut into the desired portion sizes. Bake for about 30 to ~{40%minutes}, until golden.

Leave to cool slightly before serving.